402 - By Christ Redeemed
 / 
Key: Eb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 402
Topic: Doctrines - 

Verse 1:
[Eb]By Christ redeemed, In [Bb7/D]Christ restored,
[Eb/G]We [Ab]keep [Bb/D]the [Bb7/D]memory [Bb]adored,
[Ab]And show the [Bb7/Ab]death [Ab]of [Bb7/Ab]our [Gm]dear [Eb/G]Lord,
[Bb7]Until [Eb]He come.

Verse 2:
[Eb]His broken [Gm]body [Eb]in [Bb7/D]our stead Is [Gm]here,
[Eb/G]In [Gm]this [Bb7/D]memorial [Bb]bread;
[Ab]And so our [Bb7/Ab]feeble love [Gm]is [Eb/G]fed,
[Bb7]Until [Eb]He come.

Verse 3:
[Eb]His fearful [Gm]drops [Eb]of [Bb7/D]agony,
[Eb/G]His [Ab]life [Bb/D]blood [Bb7/D]shed [Ab]for [F7/A]us [Bb]we [Eb]see;
[Ab]The wine shall [Bb7/Ab]tell [Ab]the [Bb7/Ab]mystery,
[Bb7]Until [Eb]He come.

Verse 4:
[Eb]And thus that [Fm]dark [Eb]betrayal [Bb7/Ab]night,
[Eb/G]With [Ab]the [Bb/D]last [Gm]advent [Bb]unite----
[Ab]The shame, the [Bb7/Ab]glory, by [Gm]this [Eb/G]rite,
[Bb7]Until [Eb]He come.
